==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=cassette}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|casette||dated}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|cassette}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kəˈsɛt/|/kæˈsɛt/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-cassette.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛt|æsɪt|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small flat case containing [[magnetic tape]] on two [[reel]]s, used to [[record]] and [[play back]] [[audio]] and [[video]] material.
# Any similar small [[cartridge]], such as for a computer disk or [[cassette air conditioner]]
# {{lb|en|photography}} A lightproof container for photographic [[film]].
# {{lb|en|genetics}} A [[modular]] [[DNA]] [[sequence]] encoding one or more genes for a single biochemical function.
# {{lb|en|cycling}} A set of [[sprocket]]s mounted onto a [[splined]] [[shaft]] on the [[freehub]].
# A [[saggar]] {{gloss|ceramic container used in a kiln}}

